(5054379, 736021, 83313, '<td valign="top">I have to take some of the blame for this bizarre entry. Rena and I went out taking photos of an abandoned building near downtown for this challenge. She had climbed up on the hill above the building, and I didn''t even know she had photographed an abandoned pair of tighty-whiteys. When I was looking at the shots on her memory card, I saw this. I encouraged her to submit it because it was just so offbeat and strange, it was sure to get lots of fun comments (which it did), and establish some notoriety for her.  It''s too bad this didn''t get the brown. It would have been appropriate.<br/> <br/>BTW #1, I can''t see that this is any more gross than this popular image, appropriately it was done by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=24212" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Mr_Pants</a> who gave Rena her gift membership:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=510411" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/680/120/510411.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/680/120/510411.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/680/120/510411.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>BTW #2, How does a photo of a lost pair of tighty-whitey''s come in with a higher score than <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=728734" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">"Little Red Riding Shoehorn"</a>?!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-10 15:21:27.</i></td>', 'I have to take some of the blame for this bizarre entry. Rena and I went out taking photos of an abandoned building near downtown for this challenge. She had climbed up on the hill above the building, and I didn''t even know she had photographed an abandoned pair of tighty-whiteys. When I was looking at the shots on her memory card, I saw this. I encouraged her to submit it because it was just so offbeat and strange, it was sure to get lots of fun comments (which it did), and establish some notoriety for her.  It''s too bad this didn''t get the brown. It would have been appropriate. BTW #1, I can''t see that this is any more gross than this popular image, appropriately it was done by  Mr_Pants who gave Rena her gift membership:  BTW #2, How does a photo of a lost pair of tighty-whitey''s come in with a higher score than "Little Red Riding Shoehorn"?!', '2008-11-10 00:19:24.000000', '2008-11-10 15:21:27.000000', 0),
